# Trivy ignore file for dev container images.
#
# Every entry here is a *fixed* CVE that the publish gate would otherwise block
# on but which is not exploitable in these images' actual usage. Entries are
# grouped by carrier; each group documents the carrier, why the vulnerable path
# is not exercised, and the condition under which the entry should be removed.
#
# NOT listed here, by design:
#   - linux-libc-dev (kernel-header) findings — dropped categorically by
#     .trivy/ignore-policy.rego (containers use the host kernel, not the baked-in
#     headers). Do NOT re-add kernel CVEs here; the rego covers them permanently.
#   - status=affected (no-fix) CVEs — ignore-unfixed (trivy.yaml) already keeps
#     them from gating. Only fixed findings belong in this file.
#
# Last audited: 2026-10-16 (issue #605). Fresh local arm64 builds of 17 of the
# 19 dev images were scanned without this file or the rego (ignore-unfixed and
# skip-files only), using Trivy 0.72.0 as in the CD arm64 step. 25 entries
# absent from every scan were removed. dev-go 1.25 / 1.26 do not currently
# build (go-install @latest linters need a newer Go), so the go-image-only
# entries were checked against the last published dev-go images instead and are
# kept because their go-install carriers still show them. Six new entries were
# added below, each marked with issue #605. Issue #606 then rebuilt dev-go 1.26
# locally, re-checked the go-image-only entries against it, and retired Go 1.25.
# Previous audit: 2026-08-15 (issue #561), which removed 137 stale entries.
# When re-auditing, an entry is stale if it no longer appears in a fresh scan of
# the current images (see issue #561 for the method).

# =============================================================================
# Go stdlib in the prebuilt Go tool binaries (common layer: gh, actionlint,
# nfpm, shfmt; plus scorecard, trivy, tofu on dev-base). Trivy scores Go stdlib
# vulnerabilities by the toolchain version baked into each binary, with no
# import-reachability analysis, so every stdlib CVE fixed in a Go release gates
# all of these binaries until upstream re-releases them built with the patched
# Go. They are static linters / known-host API clients operating on local files
# and outbound HTTPS to GitHub/ghcr; the affected stdlib paths (crypto/x509
# hostname check, encoding/asn1, encoding/xml, net/url, net/http h2c, crypto/tls,
# html/template, os.Root, MIME header decode) are not exercised on untrusted
# input. Remove each once the bundled tools ship binaries rebuilt with the Go
# release that fixes it (weekly bump-tools).
#
# As of the 2026-10-16 audit (issue #605), the entries in this block are
# carried only by actionlint 1.7.12 (go1.26.1, the newest release). The other
# binaries have been rebuilt with a newer Go.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-27145
CVE-2026-32280
CVE-2026-32281
CVE-2026-32283
CVE-2026-33810
CVE-2026-33811
CVE-2026-33814
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39820
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-39836
CVE-2026-42499
CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-56853
CVE-2026-56858
CVE-2026-56859
CVE-2026-56860
CVE-2026-56862

# Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 batch (issue #605). Fixed in Go 1.26.9 / 1.27.2, but the
# newest upstream release of each of these carriers is still built with an
# older Go:
#   - gh 2.102.0, go1.27.1 (GitHub CLI apt repo; all images)
#   - actionlint 1.7.12, go1.26.1 (all images)
#   - shfmt 3.14.1, go1.27.1 (all images)
#   - tofu 1.13.1, go1.27.1 (dev-base)
#   - /usr/bin/pebble, go1.26.7 (dev-java only): Canonical's Pebble service
#     manager, shipped outside dpkg in the Ubuntu 26.04 base of eclipse-temurin
#     (ubuntu:26.04 itself carries the same build). It is never started; the
#     image entrypoint is Temurin's /__cacert_entrypoint.sh.
#   - go-licenses v2.0.1 (dev-go only), CVE-2026-78669 only, via
#     golang.org/x/net v0.43.0. It is built with the image's go1.26.9, so its
#     stdlib is fixed. Issue #606.
# nfpm and trivy carried the same three CVEs. The nfpm 2.48.0 and trivy 0.76.0
# bumps fix them (both are built with go1.27.2), so those carriers are not
# ignored.
#
# CVE-2026-78667 — net/http: CPU exhaustion parsing Range headers in
#   FileServer / ServeContent / ServeFile. Server-side only. None of these
#   binaries serves files over HTTP.
# CVE-2026-97031 — crypto/tls: memory exhaustion from repeated ECH outer
#   extension references in a ClientHello. Server-side handshake only. None of
#   these binaries accepts TLS connections.
# CVE-2026-78669 — net/http HTTP/2: CPU exhaustion from repeated
#   SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE frames. Also carried as golang.org/x/net/http2
#   < 0.60.0 in gh (v0.58.0) and tofu (v0.57.0). Unlike the two above, this
#   one affects HTTP/2 clients too, and gh (api.github.com) and tofu (provider
#   and module registries) are HTTP/2 clients. Triggering it requires the
#   TLS-authenticated server itself to be malicious, and the impact is CPU
#   exhaustion of a short-lived, user-invoked CLI process, with no
#   confidentiality or integrity impact. actionlint and shfmt make no network
#   connections, and pebble never runs. In go-licenses the vulnerable
#   x/net/http2 package is not linked: the only x/net/http2 code in the binary
#   is x/net/http2/hpack (`go tool nm`), so its x/net copy cannot run the
#   HTTP/2 flow-control path at all.
#
# Remove each once gh, actionlint, shfmt, tofu and the temurin base's pebble all
# ship builds with Go >= 1.26.9 / 1.27.2 (and x/net >= 0.60.0 for gh, tofu and
# go-licenses).
# The weekly bump-tools PR and the nightly rebuild pick these up.
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-78669
CVE-2026-97031

# =============================================================================
# golang.org/x/net + x/idna vendored in the same prebuilt Go CLIs (common layer,
# all images). DNS-message SVCB/HTTPS parsing panic, IDNA Punycode label
# handling, and HTML/HTTP-parsing DoS. None of these tools acts as a DNS
# resolver, IDNA-normalizes attacker-controlled hostnames, or parses untrusted
# HTML. Remove once the bundled tools vendor the fixed x/net.
#
# As of the 2026-10-16 audit (issue #605), the carriers are actionlint 1.7.12
# (all images) and go-licenses (go image).
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-46600

# golang.org/x/net/html (go image only). Both CVEs are in the HTML parser
# (DOCTYPE character references, duplicate attributes). As of issue #606 the
# only carrier is go-licenses v2.0.1 (x/net v0.43.0, the newest release, on both
# Go images). x/net/html is not linked into that binary (`go tool nm` shows no
# x/net/html symbols), and go-licenses never parses HTML. Remove once
# go-licenses vendors x/net >= 0.55.0.
CVE-2026-25681
CVE-2026-27136

# golang.org/x/text (go image only, as of the 2026-10-16 audit: golangci-lint
# and go-licenses; the common-layer CLIs no longer carry it). norm.Iter
# infinite-loop DoS on crafted input; these tools do not normalize
# attacker-controlled text. Remove once those linters vendor x/text >= the
# fixed release.
CVE-2026-56852

# golang.org/x/image (go image only). The carrier is go-test-coverage v2.19.0,
# which pulls x/image v0.41.0 in through its coverage-badge renderer. Issue
# #606.
# CVE-2026-46602 — x/image/tiff decoder DoS (fixed in 0.43.0).
# CVE-2026-46603 — x/image/vp8l (WebP lossless) excessive allocation (fixed in
#   0.45.0).
# Neither vulnerable package is in the binary: the only x/image packages linked
# into go-test-coverage are x/image/font and x/image/math/fixed
# (`go tool nm` shows no x/image/tiff, vp8l or webp symbols), so the TIFF and
# VP8L decoders cannot run.
# Not fixable by bumping: the newest release, v2.20.0, still requires x/image
# v0.41.0 (and Go 1.27). Remove once a go-test-coverage release that builds on
# the image's Go requires x/image >= 0.45.0 (>= 0.43.0 for CVE-2026-46602).
CVE-2026-46602
CVE-2026-46603

# =============================================================================
# golang.org/x/mod < 0.40.0 vendored in the prebuilt Go CLIs. The deferred pair
# from the Go 1.26.6 / 1.25.13 batch (#559), which held them back while no
# carrier reported a vulnerable x/mod; Trivy's DB has since ingested them and
# they now gate every image. Issue #567.
#
# Vulnerable code is golang.org/x/mod/sumdb — the Go module CHECKSUM-DATABASE
# CLIENT: a malicious GOSUMDB could serve module content absent from the
# transparency log, and a coordinating GOPROXY/GOSUMDB pair could forge sumdb
# responses. Carriers: gh (all images); scorecard and tofu (dev-base); and
# goimports, go-licenses, govulncheck (go image). They vendor x/mod only to
# parse modfile / semver / module paths — none resolves dependencies through an
# attacker-controlled proxy or sumdb. Corroboration from the scans themselves:
# /usr/local/go/bin/go, the one real module client in these images, is NOT
# flagged — the toolchain already ships the patched x/mod.
#
# Not suppressed for trivy: trivy 0.74.0 vendors x/mod v0.40.0, so that carrier
# is fixed by the version bump rather than ignored (bump-tools #566).
#
# Remove per carrier as each upstream re-releases with x/mod >= 0.40.0; watch
# gh, scorecard, tofu and the go-install linters on the weekly bump.
#
# As of the 2026-10-16 audit (issue #605), gh and scorecard no longer carry a
# vulnerable x/mod. The remaining carriers are tofu 1.13.1 (x/mod v0.39.0,
# dev-base) and go-licenses v2.0.1 (x/mod v0.27.0, go image). goimports,
# golangci-lint and govulncheck carried it only in their Go 1.25 builds, which
# went away when issue #606 retired that image.
# =============================================================================
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

# google.golang.org/grpc v1.83.1 in /usr/local/bin/tofu 1.13.1 (dev-base),
# fixed in 1.83.2. Issue #605. CVE-2026-84445: a gRPC-Go server built with
# xds.NewGRPCServer panics on a request that has neither :authority nor Host.
# tofu uses gRPC only as the client of its provider plugins (go-plugin); it
# runs no xDS gRPC server. Remove once a tofu release ships grpc >= 1.83.2.
CVE-2026-84445
